course: dictionary
lesson: 9724
title: Sunburn and the sun
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sunburn is a noun. It means red, sore, hot skin caused by staying in strong sunlight too long. «Sunburned» or «sunburnt» are verb forms, and they describe skin that has been hurt by the sun.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «A boy in Queensland spent a beach day without sunscreen or a shirt; his back blistered with sunburn.» The words sore and blistered and the beach day tell you that sunburn is a painful skin injury, not a tan.
explain: Two things can happen together without one causing the other. «More ice creams and more sunburns both happen in summer, but ice cream does not cause sunburn: the sunshine causes both.» Look for the real cause in the context.
fact: Sunburn means red, sore, hot skin caused by staying in strong sunlight too long.
fact: «Sunburnt» and «sunburned» describe skin that has been hurt by the sun.
fact: The Sun's ultraviolet (UV) rays cause sunburn, even on cloudy days.
fact: Slip, Slop, Slap, Seek, Slide: slip on a shirt, slop on sunscreen, slap on a hat, seek shade, slide on sunglasses.
fact: Reapply sunscreen after swimming. Bad sunburn can blister, so you need cool water and an adult's help.
exercise: «A boy in Queensland spent a beach day without sunscreen or a shirt; his back blistered with sunburn.» What is sunburn? | A sunny day at school | *Red, sore, hot skin caused by too long in strong sunlight | A cold, wet feeling on the skin | Dark blue skin from swimming
exercise: More ice creams and more sunburns happen in summer. Does ice cream cause sunburn? | Yes, eating ice cream burns your skin | *No, the sunshine causes both | No, because ice cream is cold and cools the skin | Yes, but only in winter
exercise: Find the word that describes skin hurt by the sun. | sunbeam | suntan lotion | sunrise | *sunburned
test: Why can you get sunburn on a cloudy day? | *The Sun's UV rays can still reach your skin | Sunburn only happens in the afternoon | Cloudy days have no sunlight at all | Clouds stop the Sun from being hot
test: In «Slip, Slop, Slap, Seek, Slide», what does seek mean? | Put on sunglasses | Put on a shirt | *Find shade | Rub on sunscreen
exam: A bad sunburn can blister. What is the best thing to do? | Rub it hard with sand | Go swimming straight away | *Use cool water and ask an adult for help | Ignore it and stay in the sun
